<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Interpreting Graphs of Quadratic Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01837</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Interpreting Graphs of Quadratic Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7e8a5f1d-6918-495c-8505-9f46cef62d2d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">The height in feet, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, of a stomp rocket (propelled by a short blast of air) above the ground after <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> seconds is given by the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. Here is a graph that represents <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The x-axis represents time in seconds and the y-axis represents the height above the ground in feet. The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from 0 to 7. The y-axis scale is 50 extends from 0 to 200.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_08_09_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">How does the 5 in the equation relate to the graph?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00005">The graph intersects the vertical axis at 5.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the equation mean in terms of the rocket?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00008">It indicates that the initial velocity of the rocket was 100 feet per second upward.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">What does the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> mean in terms of the rocket?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00011">This indicates the effect of gravity pulling the rocket back toward Earth.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">About when does the rocket hit the ground?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00014">At about 6.3 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>